   "subject": "Plotting bar graph on a map",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I see a possible solution to what I want to do is geom_subplot, but that package seems to be abandoned. What I have is a CSV consisting of latitude, longitude, and magnitudes of earthquakes over the past 2 weeks and I&#39;d like to plot it on a map. What I have so far follows:<div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p><span><font size=\"1\" color=\"#000000\">require(maps)</font></span></p><p><span><font size=\"1\" color=\"#000000\">require(ggplot2)</font></span></p><p><span><font size=\"1\" color=\"#000000\">require(ggthemes)</font></span></p><p><span><font size=\"1\" color=\"#000000\">quake.data &lt;- read.csv(&#39;<a href=\"https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/feed/v1.0/summary/all_week.csv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/feed/v1.0/summary/all_week.csv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366869819000&amp;usg=AOvVaw05tOh906pVsklatbt2fzRg\">https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/feed/v1.0/summary/all_week.csv</a>&#39;)</font></span></p><p><span><font size=\"1\" color=\"#000000\">quake.data &lt;- quake.data[quake.data[,15] == &#39;earthquake&#39;,] # earthquakes only, wtf are ice quakes anyway?</font></span></p><p><span><font size=\"1\" color=\"#000000\">mapWorld &lt;- borders(&quot;world&quot;, colour=&quot;gray50&quot;, fill=&quot;gray50&quot;) # create a layer of borders</font></span></p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p><font size=\"1\" color=\"#000000\"><span>ggplot() + mapWorld + geom_point(data = quake.data, aes(x=longitude, y=latitude, colour = mag, size=mag*10)) + ggtitle(&#39;Last week quakes visualised, size of the points is the magnitude&#39;, subtitle=&#39;Source: US Geological Survey&#39;) + theme_minimal()<span>  </span>+ theme(</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">axis.title.x </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">element_blank</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">(),</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\"> axis.title.y </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">element_blank</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">())</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">+</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">scale_colour_gradient2</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">guide </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">guide_legend</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">title </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">&quot;Magnitude&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">))</span></font></p><p><font size=\"1\" color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Monaco\">Instead of geom_point, I&#39;d rather use geom_bar to create a bar representing the earthquake&#39;s magnitude. A solution seems to be to use geom_subplot[1], but that package is archived and the package&#39;s most re</span></font><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Monaco\" size=\"1\">cent fork doesn&#39;t build on R 3.4.2[2]. Any other vectors perhaps sort this? Many thanks in advance... -- H</font></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>OpenPGP: <a href=\"https://sks-keyservers.net/pks/lookup?op=get&amp;search=0xFEBAD7FFD041BBA1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://sks-keyservers.net/pks/lookup?op%3Dget%26search%3D0xFEBAD7FFD041BBA1&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366869819000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1yV0vCp6Q9JVNC4A8qv4tJ\">https://sks-keyservers.net/pks/lookup?op=get&amp;search=0xFEBAD7FFD041BBA1</a></div><div>If you wish to request my time, please do so using <a href=\"http://bit.ly/hd1ScheduleRequest\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://bit.ly/hd1ScheduleRequest&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366869819000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2zfmdKm1mBR4mEhKO0FXZc\">http://bit.ly/hd1ScheduleRequest</a>.</div><div><font color=\"#222222\">Si vous voudrais faire connnaisance, allez a <a href=\"http://bit.ly/hd1ScheduleRequest\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://bit.ly/hd1ScheduleRequest&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366869819000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2zfmdKm1mBR4mEhKO0FXZc\">http://bit.ly/hd1ScheduleRequest</a>.</font></div><div><font color=\"#222222\"><a href=\"https://sks-keyservers.net/pks/lookup?op=get&amp;search=0xFEBAD7FFD041BBA1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://sks-keyservers.net/pks/lookup?op%3Dget%26search%3D0xFEBAD7FFD041BBA1&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366869819000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1yV0vCp6Q9JVNC4A8qv4tJ\"><font color=\"#222222\"><br></font></a></font>Sent from my mobile device</div><div>Envoye de mon portable</div><div>1. <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/16028659/plotting-bar-charts-on-map-using-ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://stackoverflow.com/questions/16028659/plotting-bar-charts-on-map-using-ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792366869819000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1zsCA0hLY7_nSPK6qXU2JF\">https://stackoverflow.com/questions/16028659/plotting-bar-charts-on-map-using-ggplot2</a></div><div>2. <a href=\"https://github.com/garrettgman/ggsubplot/issues/17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/garret